#!args apps/JFNetworker/tests/fixtures/script_kv.jfnet --scenario apps/JFNetworker/tests/scen/script_kv.scn --golden apps/JFNetworker/tests/scen/script_kv.report
# golden scenario of scripts as services: a key-value store written as a script (kv.jfs in the
# fixture) on SRV1 behind a load generator, its fuel the CPU time of one thread (100 ns per
# instruction, about 1.1 ms per request): 200 requests per second take about a fifth of the
# CPU, 1500 per second fill the queue to 100 and get 503 beyond it, the latency climbs to tens
# of milliseconds; a second script on MON polls the numbers with http.request every second
# (script, script status, script output, top, curl in the report).  The GUI program runs
# tests/scen/script_kv.scn on tests/fixtures/script_kv.jfnet without a window and ends with
# the report, which must equal tests/scen/script_kv.report byte for byte on every target (the
# script itself is not run)
